# Brain Sync Protocol (Cross-Thread)

## Problem Statement
Work done in Thread A isn't visible to Thread B because:
1. Each Claude Desktop thread has independent MCP connection
2. Manual [brain_emit_event()](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#2439-2443) calls are inconsistent
3. [task.md](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/.gemini/antigravity/brain/7c654df4-b83e-43f9-8620-f15868ec39d1/task.md) updates happen but events don't always fire

## Solution: Automatic Event Emission

### Phase 1: Antigravity Hook (Client-Side)
Make Antigravity ALWAYS log significant actions:

```python
# In Antigravity's internal system
def on_file_edit(file_path, change_type):
    # Automatic event emission
    brain_emit_event(
        event_type="file_modified",
        emitter="antigravity",
        data={"file": file_path, "type": change_type}
    )

def on_task_complete(task_name):
    # Automatic Brain update
    brain_update_task(task_name, {"status": "DONE"})
    brain_emit_event(
        event_type="task_completed",
        emitter="antigravity",
        data={"task": task_name}
    )
```

### Phase 2: MCP Server Hook (Server-Side)
Add automatic logging to Nucleus MCP tools:

```python
# In mcp-server-nucleus/__init__.py
@mcp.tool()
def brain_update_task(task_id: str, updates: dict):
    result = _update_task(task_id, updates)
    
    # AUTOMATIC EVENT EMISSION
    _emit_event(
        event_type="task_state_changed",
        emitter="nucleus_mcp",
        data={"task_id": task_id, "updates": updates}
    )
    
    return result
```

### Phase 3: File Watcher (Background Sync)
Run a background process that watches Brain files:

```python
# scripts/brain_sync.py
import time
from watchdog.observers import Observer
from watchdog.events import FileSystemEventHandler

class BrainSyncHandler(FileSystemEventHandler):
    def on_modified(self, event):
        if event.src_path.endswith("task.md"):
            # Emit event when task.md changes
            emit_event("task_file_modified")
```

